    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0161" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/6–2846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-11T19:00:00-04:00">July 11, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>923. Embtel 1733 June 28.<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d112-f1"/> Restrictions on shipments first quarter allocation of 578
                    tons natural rubber already lifted. Dept has repeatedly requested Braz to concur in shipment of 1250 tons second
                    quarter allocation awaiting shipment.</p>
                <p>CRC has allocated 2300 tons natural from UK plus 200 tons butyl from Canada for Arg for third quarter. This action proposed and
                    supported by US. These shipments not subject to concurrence Braz under tripartite agreement. Hence should soon
                    allow Arg domestic production to operate near
                    capacity. (Re Embtel 1671 June 21) <pb
                        facs="0162" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/> Question of 60,000 passenger and 12,000
                    truck tires from US depends on cancellation of tripartite agreement or
                    concurrence Braz in shipment. Estimate of
                    supply for Arg will be established when
                    concurrence obtained if supply permits. OIT
                    prefers not to withhold large contingency reserve to cover possible Arg quota if tripartite agreement is going to
                    prevent licensing during most of third quarter.</p>
                <p>Sent to Buenos Aires, rptd to Rio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
